<https://culturalcartography.net/names/eli-whitney/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Eli Whitney" ;
    dcterms:description "Silliman was a friend of Whitney's for 25 years, starting at Yale; in a memoir he wrote eloquently of Whitney's ingenuity. Morse painted his distant cousin Whitney's portrait in 1821, when both were neighbours near Yale. While Whitney exchanged letters with Thomas Jefferson about a patent, there is more myth-making than clear evidence to suggest that the relationship passed beyond the functional and formal."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.eliwhitney.org/inventor.htm> ;
