<https://culturalcartography.net/names/evariste-galois/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Évariste Galois" ;
    dcterms:description "Cauchy received from Galois, still in his teens, a memoir on equation theory, and was impressed enough to suggest he send it to Fourier so it could be considered for a prize. However Fourier died and the moment was lost. Poisson later invited Galois to send a copy to him, but found it unclear, and by the time Galois received the response, he was in prison for revolutionary activities (and died very soon after, after a duel and in unclear circumstances)."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Evariste-Galois> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q7091 ;
    foaf:familyName "Galois" ;
    foaf:givenName "Évariste" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/evariste-galois/>,
        <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evariste_Galois> ;
    foaf:knows <https://culturalcartography.net/names/augustin-louis-cauchy/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/simeon-denis-poisson/#person> ;
    foaf:name "Évariste Galois" ;
    wkw:birthPlaceText "Bourg-La-Reine, France" ;
    wkw:datesText "1811 (Bourg-La-Reine, France) – 1832 (Paris)" ;
    wkw:deathPlaceText "Paris" ;
    wkw:sortKey "Galois, Evariste" ;
    wkw:status "bio" ;
    wkw:wordpressId 3519 ;
    schema:birthDate "1811"^^xsd:gYear ;
    schema:deathDate "1832"^^xsd:gYear ;
    schema:hasOccupation <https://culturalcartography.net/professions/mathematician/#concept> .

<https://culturalcartography.net/names/farkas-bolyai/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Farkas Bolyai" ;
    dcterms:description "Bolyai and Gauss met as students in Göttingen. Bolyai had gone to Germany to study; they became lifelong friends. After Bolyai returned home, his life had few consolations other than his own work and his continuing correspondence with Gauss, even his relationship with his mathematician son János being a difficult one; he spoke about a \"permanently overcast sky\" after the promise of \"beautiful days\" in Germany."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www-history.mcs.st-andrews.ac.uk/Biographies/Bolyai_Farkas.html> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q252311 ;
    skos:altLabel "Wolfgang Bolyai" ;
    foaf:familyName "Bolyai" ;
    foaf:givenName "Farkas" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/farkas-bolyai/>,
        <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Farkas_Bolyai> ;
    foaf:knows <https://culturalcartography.net/names/carl-friedrich-gauss/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/janos-bolyai/#person> ;
    foaf:name "Farkas Bolyai" ;
    wkw:birthPlaceText "Bolya, Hungary, now Buia, Romania" ;
    wkw:datesText "1775 (Bolya, Hungary, now Buia, Romania) – 1856 (Marosvásáhrely, now Târgu Mureş)" ;
    wkw:deathPlaceText "Marosvásáhrely, now Târgu Mureş" ;
    wkw:notToBeConfusedWith <https://culturalcartography.net/names/janos-bolyai/#person> ;
    wkw:sortKey "Bolyai, Farkas" ;
    wkw:status "bio" ;
    wkw:wordpressId 3211 ;
    schema:birthDate "1775"^^xsd:gYear ;
    schema:deathDate "1856"^^xsd:gYear ;
    schema:hasOccupation <https://culturalcartography.net/professions/mathematician/#concept> .

