    rdfs:label "Padre Antonio Soler" ;
    dcterms:description "Soler got to know Scarlatti in his early twenties, when both were based at El Escorial. It is generally understood that Soler studied with Scarlatti; he certainly referred to himself as Scarlatti's disciple, and is regarded as his most important one. He corresponded with Martini about Martini's controversial (in its day) treatise on harmony."@en ;
