<https://culturalcartography.net/names/andre-francois/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "André François" ;
    dcterms:description "François studied with Cassandre and then worked in his studio. He was a close friend of Searle's, as well as collaborating with him. When working with Prévert, they used to meet in a café to discuss the text and images for a children's book that at the same time referred subversively to the then German occupation of France."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.nytimes.com/2005/04/15/arts/design/andre-francois-is-dead-at-89-illustrator-with-biting-satire.html>,
        <https://www.theguardian.com/news/2005/apr/21/guardianobituaries.france> ;
