<https://culturalcartography.net/names/noah-webster/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Noah Webster" ;
    dcterms:description "Webster was a neighbour of the Morse family in the Boston region: Morse painted the lexicographer's portrait (did they also discuss ways words might be transcribed?). Franklin and Webster had a lengthy correspondence about rationalised spelling, a subject close to each man's heart. The poet Trumbull feared Webster would \"dine upon dissertations, and go to bed supperless.\""@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://noahwebsterhouse.org/noahwebsterhistory/>,
        <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Noah-Webster-American-lexicographer> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q241676 ;
