<https://culturalcartography.net/names/joseph-le-conte/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Joseph Le Conte" ;
    dcterms:description "Le Conte studied with Gray and Agassiz, and accompanied Agassiz on expeditions. He moved to California in fear of post-Civil-War politics in the southern states (he was not a supporter of racial equality), and befriended Muir, with whom he helped found the Sierra Club; perhaps fittingly, Le Conte died in Yosemite."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.fampeople.com/cat-joseph-leconte>,
        <https://www.uh.edu/engines/epi2212.htm> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q3810237 ;
