<https://culturalcartography.net/names/alain/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Alain" ;
    dcterms:description "Aron, Canguilhem, Weil and Maurois were all taught by the self-effacing Alain (the pen-name by which Émile-Auguste Chartier is better-known): Canguilhem was strongly influenced by him, while Weil credited him as having had a lasting effect on her philosophy, especially regarding political thought. Alain was one among Rolland's vast circle of correspondents."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://danassays.wordpress.com/encyclopedia-of-the-essay/alain-emile-auguste-chartier/>,
        <https://tlrdoc.free.fr/pages/phda.htm> ;
