<https://culturalcartography.net/names/claude-lanzmann/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Lanzmann" ;
    dcterms:description "Lanzmann was befriended by his elders Sartre and de Beauvoir, then started working on their review 'Les Temps Modernes' (which Lanzmann published after their demise). He had a long affair with de Beauvoir, staying close to her until her death: she worked with him on his landmark film 'Shoah.' He met Fanon in North Africa and acted as emissary between him and Sartre (his planned book about Fanon, following Fanon's death, came to nothing). Lanzmann worked with Ophüls on his film about Klaus Barbie. Tournier and he had met as students from France in post-war Germany, studying philosophy in Tübingen."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Claude-Lanzmann>,
        <https://www.jacobinmag.com/2018/07/claude-lanzmann-shoah-holocaust-antisemitism>,
        <https://www.theguardian.com/film/2018/jul/05/claude-lanzmann-obituary> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q551512 ;
    foaf:familyName "Lanzmann" ;
    foaf:givenName "Claude" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/claude-lanzmann/>,
        <https://fr.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_Lanzmann> ;
