<https://culturalcartography.net/names/r-d-laing/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "R. D. Laing" ;
    dcterms:description "As a psychiatrist associated with the anti-psychiatry movement, Laing remains controversial. Winnicott and Bowlby were senior colleagues at the Tavistock Clinic in London; Winnicott was his supervisor, and responded warmly to Laing's 'The Divided Self'. Trocchi, a fellow-Glaswegian and counter-cultural icon, counted Laing among his associates; Laing gave Leary his first shot of heroin in Trocchi's house. He met Bateson, another important collaborator who also acquired counter-cultural status, in the U.S."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.britannica.com/biography/R-D-Laing>,
        <https://www.encyclopedia.com/people/medicine/psychology-and-psychiatry-biographies/r-d-laing> ;
