<https://culturalcartography.net/names/serge-gainsbourg/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Serge Gainsbourg" ;
    dcterms:description "Léger briefly taught Gainsbourg, before he turned to music. He became Vian's protégé — they met while Gainsbourg was working as a piano-player in a bar. Under Vian's influence, he stirred together Baudelairean poetry and oblique jazz in the vein of chanson. Gréco invited the young Gainsbourg to write for her — several hits resulted. Brel, originally met while both were touring a popular stage-show, suggested he sing his compositions more himself, rather than writing for others."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.musicianguide.com/biographies/1608003567/Serge-Gainsbourg.html>,
        <https://www.theguardian.com/books/2001/feb/02/culture.features> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q1698 ;
    foaf:familyName "Gainsbourg" ;
    foaf:givenName "Serge" ;
