        <https://culturalcartography.net/professions/explorer/#concept> .

<https://culturalcartography.net/names/alcide-dorbigny/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Alcide d'Orbigny" ;
    dcterms:description "Despite d'Orbigny's obsolete ideas (including that there had been 28 creations of life, and 27 total extinctions), much of his detailed work has had continued relevance. Audubon was a childhood friend in France (d'Orbigny's father gave him drawing lessons). Cuvier and Geoffroy taught him, and were responsible for the seven-year South American expedition he undertook (Cuvier died while he was away). Humboldt, met in Paris (and whose colleague Bonpland was a family friend of the d'Orbigny's), correctly asserted that the funds for the expedition wouldn't be enough. Darwin corresponded though never met him, and thought his work second only to Humboldt's."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.strangescience.net/dorbigny.htm> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q344661 ;
    foaf:familyName "d'Orbigny" ;
    foaf:givenName "Alcide" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/alcide-dorbigny/>,
        <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alcide_d'Orbigny> ;
    foaf:knows <https://culturalcartography.net/names/alexander-von-humboldt/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/charles-darwin/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/esprit-requien/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/geoffroy-saint-hilaire/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/georges-cuvier/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/john-james-audubon/#person> ;
    foaf:name "Alcide d'Orbigny" ;
    wkw:birthPlaceText "Couëron, France" ;
    wkw:datesText "1802 (Couëron, France) – 1857 (Pierrefitte-sur-Seine)" ;
    wkw:deathPlaceText "Pierrefitte-sur-Seine" ;
    wkw:sortKey "Dorbigny, Alcide" ;
    wkw:status "bio" ;
