<https://culturalcartography.net/names/carl-friedrich-von-martius/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Carl Friedrich von Martius" ;
    dcterms:description "Martius spent three years travelling extensively in Brazil, collecting botanical and other specimens; Spix was his zoologist companion for much of these explorations. Schweinitz was among those to whom Martius sent specimens he'd collected. Agassiz, Schimpel and Braun all studied with Martius in Munich; Cuvier suggested Agassiz catalogue Martius' collection of Brazilian fish (which he proceeded to do in Latin)."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.wku.edu/~smithch/chronob/MART1794.htm> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q77131 ;
    skos:editorialNote "Dates were '1814 (Erlangen, Germany) – 1868 (Munich)': Born 1794 not 1814"@en ;
