<https://culturalcartography.net/names/john-wilkinson/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "John Wilkinson" ;
    dcterms:description "Wilkinson's technological advances made him an influential pioneer of the use of cast iron, and a significant developer of precision machine tools. He was a generous supporter of Priestley (married to Wilkinson's sister), and had a close working relationship with Watt and Boulton, until Watt discovered he was pirating his own steam-engine designs. He supported Telford, and worked with Darby in the construction of the world's first iron bridge. Young joined Watt and Wilkinson to help choose the design for a new London Bridge. While many of Wilkinson's innovations were widely influential, his cast-iron shoes did not catch on."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.bbc.co.uk/history/historic_figures/wilkinson_john.shtml>,
        <https://www.britannica.com/biography/John-Wilkinson> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q1204884 ;
