<https://culturalcartography.net/names/marcel-carne/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Marcel Carné" ;
    dcterms:description "Carné was a significant director of films from the 1930's to the 1950's. Jacques Prévert was his great collaborator, writing scripts for his most celebrated and poetic films. Kosma was also a noted collaborator. Barrault and Brel acted for him, Boiffard shot stills. Early in his career, Clair had given him a foot up, engaging him as second assistant director."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.imdb.com/name/nm0138893/bio>,
