<https://culturalcartography.net/names/henri-chopin/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Henri Chopin" ;
    dcterms:description "Chopin (not the composer Frédéric) recorded Hausmann performing old Dada sound-works in the 1950's, was in a show together with Gysin, and published his work. Heidsieck was a friend and fellow-founder of 'Domaine Poétique'. Cobbing was among guests at Chopin's house in Essex, Burroughs a correspondent, and Finlay among his collaborators."@en ;
