<https://culturalcartography.net/names/jacques-brel/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Jacques Brel" ;
    dcterms:description "Supreme figure in French-language chanson. When he was still struggling to make headway and had come next to last in a competition, Gréco (who described him as raw-boned and untamed) asked if she could sing one of his songs. Both subsequently quit their record labels to join Barclay's; Barclay became a true friend. Brel acted in films by Carné and Lelouch, took part in a legendary radio interview with his friend Brassens and Ferré, and advised Gainsbourg to sing more himself. Aznavour, another friend, tried in vain to persuade him not to retire from singing."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Jacques-Brel>,
        <https://www.jacquesbrel.be/en/my-life/brief-biography>,
        <https://www.rfimusique.com/siteen/biographie/biographie_6099.asp> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q1666 ;
