<https://culturalcartography.net/names/berenice-abbott/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Berenice Abbott" ;
    dcterms:description "In her early bohemian days in New York she met Millay (whether they really had an affair is unknown) and posed for Ray. Barnes and Burke shared a house with her. Later in Paris, she became Ray's assistant — he wanted someone who knew nothing about photography. Through him she befriended Atget, photo'd him, found he'd died when she took the prints around, and made it a lifetime project to get his work known. Noguchi sculpted her head, she photographed him (and many other art-world notables). She and Strand established the radically-oriented Photo League back in New York."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://nmwa.org/explore/artist-profiles/berenice-abbott>,
        <https://www.icp.org/browse/archive/constituents/berenice-abbott?all/all/all/all/0> ;
