<https://culturalcartography.net/names/bernard-heidsieck/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Bernard Heidsieck" ;
    dcterms:description "Heidsieck's role in establishing sound poetry in France is significant; his use of tape-recording was especially innovative. His key professional friendship was with Chopin; they were founder members of the mixed-media group 'Domaine Poétique'. Giorno was also a friend (he helped Heidsieck record the sound of his bank's computers), Rivers (on sax) his sole collaborator, Schneemann among many visitors. He sent a 'sound-letter' to Gysin, ill in London. Ashbery took him to supper with Saint Phalle and Tinguely, who grilled meat on a kinetic sculpture. A banker by day, one of his friends described him as a disciplined anarchist."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.erratum.org/old/heidsieck/index.html>,
        <https://www.telegraph.co.uk/news/obituaries/11462168/Bernard-Heidsieck-sound-poet-obituary.html>,
        <https://www.thewire.co.uk/news/34223/french-sound-poet-bernard-heidsieck-dies> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q2718788 ;
    foaf:familyName "Heidsieck" ;
    foaf:givenName "Bernard" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/bernard-heidsieck/> ;
