<https://culturalcartography.net/names/charles-de-montesquieu/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Charles de Montesquieu" ;
    dcterms:description "Montesquieu contributed articles to Diderot's Encyclopédie and was a close friend, though he avoided over-familiarity with Parisian circles. He visited Swift and Pope during a visit to England, and corresponded with Montagu. His good friend Helvétius tried to dissuade him from publishing some of his opinions, and kept quiet when the book became a public success. Montesquieu was a regular guest of d'Épinay."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://plato.stanford.edu/entries/montesquieu/> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q15975 ;
    skos:altLabel "Montesquieu" ;
