<https://culturalcartography.net/names/joseph-addison/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Joseph Addison" ;
    dcterms:description "Addison is noteworthy for his extremely influential journalistic collaborations with Steele (a classic partnership of opposites: Addison quiet and scholarly, Steele noisily confident). He first met Swift in Ireland, and addressed a poem to Dryden, who became a friend. Leibniz was met in Berlin – Addison later wrote seeking a drawing of a bison. Tonson helped preside over the camaraderie that bound a notable literary gang together. Montagu wrote a criticism of his hit play 'Cato' that he asked her not to publish, though he adopted most improvements she suggested. Pope, a former friend (introduced by Steele), later satirised him."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://virginia-anthology.org/joseph-addison-and-richard-steele/>,
        <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Joseph-Addison> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q206384 ;
