<https://culturalcartography.net/names/louis-jean-marie-daubenton/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Louis Jean-Marie Daubenton" ;
    dcterms:description "Though less renowned than Buffon (a childhood friend and professional colleague, who got him in because of his own distaste for anatomy and dissection), Daubenton was a significant naturalist and a pioneer of comparative anatomy. He contributed to Diderot's encyclopaedia, wrote a preface for Lamarck, taught and inspired Haüy, and knew Banks. He recommended Geoffroy — who had attended his lectures and was also supported by another of Daubenton's protégés, Vicq d'Azyr — to an important first job. After a decade working together, Buffon excised his contribution to the 'Histoire Naturelle' (to its detriment), though they later made up."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Louis-Jean-Marie-Daubenton>,
        <https://www.lindahall.org/louis-jean-marie-daubenton/> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q546443 ;
    foaf:familyName "Daubenton" ;
    foaf:givenName "Louis Jean-Marie" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/louis-jean-marie-daubenton/>,
        <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louis-Jean-Marie_Daubenton> ;
    foaf:knows <https://culturalcartography.net/names/bernard-germain-de-lacepede/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/comte-de-buffon/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/denis-diderot/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/etienne-geoffroy-saint-hilaire/#person>,
