<https://culturalcartography.net/names/bernard-de-jussieu/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Bernard de Jussieu" ;
    dcterms:description "Jussieu, a modest man, developed a naming system for plants that, unlike Linnaeus's, was morphologically-based. Trained in medicine, he went with his elder brother (already a botanist) on a research trip to Spain, developing there into a botanist himself. Lamarck (his student and assistant for 18 years), Lavoisier and Guettard all studied with him; Buffon and Duhamel du Monceau were Jardin des Plantes colleagues. Sloane and Linnaeus (who attended his lectures and greatly respected him) corresponded. Réaumur prompted his investigation of fresh-water polyps (which he correctly identified as animal), while Antoine-Laurent de Jussieu was his nephew and successor."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Bernard-de-Jussieu>,
        <https://www.encyclopedia.com/science/dictionaries-thesauruses-pictures-and-press-releases/jussieu-bernard-de> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q432734 ;
    foaf:familyName "Jussieu" ;
    foaf:givenName "Bernard de" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/bernard-de-jussieu/> ;
    foaf:knows <https://culturalcartography.net/names/antoine-laurent-de-jussieu/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/antoine-lavoisier/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/carl-linnaeus/#person>,
