<https://culturalcartography.net/names/christian-felix-weisse/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Christian Felix Weisse" ;
    dcterms:description "Mendelssohn told him that he wrote with too much facility; Goethe reported that everyone liked him and enthusiastically enjoyed his plays. What they and others disregarded was his importance, in hindsight, as a children's author and writer of popular lyrics. Lessing and he were close friends as students, scrounging for a living, and translating plays. Klopstock was another student friend. Hiller collaborated with him on a number of light operas (they more or less invented German singspiel). Wieland and Jean Paul visited him; he also got acquainted with Rousseau and Voltaire when he was in Paris."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.bookrags.com/biography/christian-felix-weisse-dlb/> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q68815 ;
    foaf:familyName "Weisse" ;
    foaf:givenName "Christian Felix" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/christian-felix-weisse/>,
        <https://de.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Felix_Weiße>,
        <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Felix_Weiße> ;
    foaf:knows <https://culturalcartography.net/names/christoph-martin-wieland/#person>,
