<https://culturalcartography.net/names/jean-philippe-rameau/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Jean-Philippe Rameau" ;
    dcterms:description "Voltaire was both friend and collaborator, working with Rameau on a comedy ballet and several operas. Martini was a correspondent. Boucher, Crébillon and Piron were fellow-members of a singing club: Piron co-wrote a comic opera with him. Diderot and d'Alembert had been friends, but Rameau's disputatiousness over the Encyclopédie's treatment of French music made good relations difficult; He had a major spat with Rousseau, who had written the entry."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.allmusic.com/artist/jean-philippe-rameau-mn0000930018/biography>,
        <https://www.newworldencyclopedia.org/entry/Jean-Philippe_Rameau> ;
