<https://culturalcartography.net/names/margaret-mead/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Margaret Mead" ;
    dcterms:description "Boas (who was hugely influential) and Benedict taught Mead, Benedict in particular becoming a lifelong friend and, it is now accepted, sometime lover. Sapir, Benedict and Mead shared a love of poetry, reading and commenting on each others' verse. Hurston was also a professional colleague, while Baldwin collaborated on a book about race. Bateson was her third husband, whose photo she kept by her until death; Lévi-Strauss (then lesser-known than her) met her when he exiled himself in New York; Maslow regarded her as his mentor."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://authorscalendar.info/mmead.htm>,
        <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Margaret-Mead> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q180099 ;
