<https://culturalcartography.net/names/andrei-bely/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Andrei Bely" ;
    dcterms:description "Bely was Boris Bugaev's pen-name. Tsvetaeva, then an emergent writer, met him in the circle around the critic Voloshin. Ehrenburg, Mayakovsky, Mandelstam and Pasternak were others he hob-nobbed with; Pasternak said he hadn't stretched his talent as much as he should have, but also acknowledged his influence. Bryusov co-edited a magazine with him, Bakst painted him. He had a close but stormy friendship with Blok, his fellow-follower of the esoteric philosopher Solovyov, having an affair with Blok's wife, and duelling with him. Bely became a disciple of Steiner's, working on his anthroposophical temple in Switzerland, before falling out with him."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://russiapedia.rt.com/prominent-russians/literature/andrey-bely/> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q212632 ;
    skos:altLabel "Boris Nikolaevich Bugaev" ;
