<https://culturalcartography.net/names/christoph-willibald-von-gluck/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Christoph Willibald von Gluck" ;
    dcterms:description "Sammartini, who taught him, became a very close friend. Salieri, a friend from Vienna, went to Paris with him, where they presented a successful opera as a collaboration before coming clean and announcing that the music was all Salieri's. He so liked an opera of Mozart's that he invited him to dinner — Mozart's father had earlier told him to avoid Gluck. He visited Italy with Dittersdorf, and met Handel in London (possibly Garrick too, whose acting style strongly impressed him): he so revered Handel that he kept a portrait of him in his bedroom, though Handel said Gluck knew no more about music than his cook."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.allmusic.com/artist/christoph-willibald-gluck-mn0001649323/biography> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q130759 ;
    foaf:familyName "Gluck" ;
    foaf:givenName "Christoph Willibald von" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/christoph-willibald-von-gluck/>,
