<https://culturalcartography.net/names/umberto-eco/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Umberto Eco" ;
    dcterms:description "Pareyson and Abbagnano taught Eco; Vattimo was a fellow-student. Eco's long friendship with Berio started when both worked for the Italian state broadcaster, RAI. Hobsbawm and Putnam were academic colleagues-in-arms. Eco held Calvino in high regard, corresponded with Quine, conversed with Wilson, and described Barthes as \"my dear friend.\""@en ;
