<https://culturalcartography.net/names/francis-ponge/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Francis Ponge" ;
    dcterms:description "Ponge got to know Picasso, Braque, Giacometti and Hélion — artists he liked to spend time with — through Leiris (whom he accompanied to Algeria). Paulhan published him, but years of delays muddied the waters of their friendship. Duras' apartment was home to a circle of writers and intellectuals, Ponge among them. Camus sent him the manuscript of 'The Myth of Sysiphus', and started a rich correspondence. Paulhan introduced him and Dubuffet to each other, and Sollers published an interview with him."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poets/francis-ponge> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q551749 ;
