<https://culturalcartography.net/names/roger-vitrac/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Roger Vitrac" ;
    dcterms:description "Vitrac met Crevel, Arland and Limbourt on military service; together, they founded a literary review. Breton and Aragon were among Vitrac's surrealistic circle of friends; Éluard and Boiffard co-wrote with him the preface to the first edition of 'la Révolution surréaliste.' Artaud and he, defecting from Breton's orbit (having quarrelled with him), founded a short-lived theatre company together. Becoming one of Bataille's associates, Vitrac contributed to his review 'Documents', and co-signed a polemic directed against Breton. He wrote a critical study of de Chirico's work, and referred to the more successful Anouilh as his 'spiritual brother.'"@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.premiere.fr/Star/Roger-Vitrac> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q809732 ;
    foaf:familyName "Vitrac" ;
    foaf:givenName "Roger" ;
