<https://culturalcartography.net/names/anne-robert-jacques-turgot/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Anne Robert Jacques Turgot" ;
    dcterms:description "He was one of the most noted contributors to Diderot and d'Alembert's Encyclopédie, writing on etymology, physics and philosophy as well as economics. Condorcet was a protégé and long-term friend, while Voltaire became one of his main supporters, praising his translations from Virgil. Smith knew him from d'Holbach's, became a close friend, and almost certainly owed some of his own ideas to conversations with him. Michel Turgot was his father, who as 'mayor' was responsible for a series of classic maps of Paris."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://mises.org/library/biography-arj-turgot-1727-1781-brief-lucid-and-brilliant>,
        <https://www.econlib.org/library/Enc1/bios/Turgot.html> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q221303 ;
