<https://culturalcartography.net/names/dante-gabriel-rossetti/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Dante Gabriel Rossetti" ;
    dcterms:description "Christina was his sister, while Cotman taught him at school. He studied with Brown, tiring of his teaching but staying friends for life. The friendship with Hunt was critical — together with Millais they forged the Pre-Raphaelite philosophy. Further significant friendships began when Rossetti met Morris and Burne-Jones with both still students (even though Rossetti's technical shortcomings soon showed). Tennyson, Browning and Whistler were friends, and Ruskin a keen but critical patron. Rossetti was a strong and tolerant influence on Swinburne, given the poet's excesses when they shared a house in Chelsea."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.poetryfoundation.org/poets/dante-gabriel-rossetti>,
        <https://www.victorianweb.org/authors/dgr/dgrseti13.html> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q186748 ;
    foaf:familyName "Rossetti" ;
    foaf:givenName "Dante Gabriel" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/dante-gabriel-rossetti/>,
        <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dante_Gabriel_Rossetti> ;
    foaf:knows <https://culturalcartography.net/names/alfred-lord-tennyson/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/algernon-charles-swinburne/#person>,
        <https://culturalcartography.net/names/christina-rossetti/#person>,
