<https://culturalcartography.net/names/georges-canguilhem/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Georges Canguilhem" ;
    dcterms:description "Alain (Émile Chartier) taught him; Sartre, Nizan and Aron were fellow-students. Cavaillès encouraged him to join the resistance during WWII. Bachelard taught alongside him. Deleuze and Bourdieu studied under him; he sponsored Foucault's doctoral thesis on the history of madness, and advised Derrida to establish himself seriously before indulging in intellectual humour. Althusser declared that his debt to Canguilhem was incalculable."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.independent.co.uk/news/people/obituary-georges-canguilhem-1601992.html>,
        <https://www.radicalphilosophy.com/obituary/georges-canguilhem-1904-1995> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q433741 ;
