<https://culturalcartography.net/names/raymond-aron/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Raymond Aron" ;
    dcterms:description "Sartre, Nizan and Aron all met at school: Canguilhem joined them at the École Nationale Supérieur. Sartre, de Beauvoir and Merleau-Ponty were among Aron's co-founders of the review 'Les Temps modernes.' Camus edited another journal, 'Combat', with him. He was taught by Alain (the pen-name of Émile Chartier), while Bourdieu became his teaching assistant. He worked briefly with Malraux; Arendt became a friend when she fled Nazi Germany. He said that if his fellow-student Cavaillès had survived, he (Aron) would not have committed so many errors."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://contemporarythinkers.org/raymond-aron/biography/>,
        <https://www.encyclopedia.com/people/social-sciences-and-law/sociology-biographies/raymond-aron> ;
