<https://culturalcartography.net/names/alain-resnais/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Alain Resnais" ;
    dcterms:description "Resnais engaged in deep collaborations with a number of writers, most notably Duras, Robbe-Grillet and Cayrol — all personal friends. He met the 16-year-old Truffaut (whose first film Resnais edited) at a film-club run by Bazin. Eisler (whom he didn't dare to expect a contribution from) travelled to Paris to work on the music for 'Nuit et Brouillard.' Resnais married Malraux's daughter — Malraux claimed 'Hiroshima Mon Amour' to be the most beautiful film he'd ever seen. Resnais edited for Varda, co-directed with his friend Marker, and made a film about polystyrene with Queneau."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.allmovie.com/artist/alain-resnais-p108005>,
        <https://www.theguardian.com/film/2014/mar/02/alain-resnais> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q218022 ;
    foaf:familyName "Resnais" ;
    foaf:givenName "Alain" ;
