<https://culturalcartography.net/names/johann-friedrich-blumenbach/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Johann Friedrich Blumenbach" ;
    dcterms:description "Blumenbach effectively invented anthropology and (with Vicq d'Azyr) comparative anatomy; some later followers ignored his increasingly enlightened ideas about racial classification. As a student he was employed by Heyne (his future brother-in-law) to organise his natural history collection. Haller was a mentor, Goethe and Kant friends (Blumenbach refuted Kant's ideas of European superiority), as were Lichtenberg and Forster (who together published important work of his). He taught Humboldt, Sömmering and Lawrence; Coleridge also met him and attended his lectures. Banks, another friend, sent him skulls for his collection."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://embryo.asu.edu/pages/johann-friedrich-blumenbach-1752-1840>,
        <https://www.whonamedit.com/doctor.cfm/1247.html> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q58588 ;
    foaf:familyName "Blumenbach" ;
    foaf:givenName "Johann Friedrich" ;
    foaf:isPrimaryTopicOf <https://culturalcartography.net/names/johann-friedrich-blumenbach/>,
        <https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Johann_Friedrich_Blumenbach> ;
