<https://culturalcartography.net/names/camille-saint-saens/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Camille Saint-Saëns" ;
    dcterms:description "Halévy taught him. His close friend Berlioz famously said that the then-young composer knew everything, but lacked inexperience. Liszt (an influence, and a lifelong friend), Gounod, Rossini and Berlioz all admired him for his gifts. Fauré was his favourite pupil: after the death of Saint-Saëns' own two children, he acted as 'second father' to Fauré's. Bizet and Doré were friends (Liszt and he played together in Doré's house.) Saint-Saëns loved Hugo's poetry, set it to music, and met him more than once. He helped Widor to an important position, and in Moscow improvised a ballet with Tchaikovsky (Saint-Saëns in drag.)"@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.allmusic.com/artist/camille-saint-saëns-mn0000688311/biography> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q150445 ;
    foaf:familyName "Saint-Saëns" ;
    foaf:givenName "Camille" ;
