<https://culturalcartography.net/names/phil-spector/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Phil Spector" ;
    dcterms:description "Spector was one of the most inventive and influential of record producers, and remains notorious for his anti-social behaviour. He learned on the job with Leiber and Stoller (co-writing 'Spanish Harlem' with Leiber) and then with Ertegun. As a writer he collaborated with Goffin and King and with Greenwich and Barry, the latter two providing him with the raw material for a string of hit singles. He took the young Wilson under his wing; Jagger and Richards also hung around profitably. He supposedly threatened both Lennon and Cohen at pistol-point, and attempted to exclude Cohen and Turner from work in hand."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.allmusic.com/artist/phil-spector-mn0000694967/biography>,
        <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Phil-Spector>,
        <https://www.rockhall.com/inductees/phil-spector> ;
