<https://culturalcartography.net/names/norman-mailer/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Norman Mailer" ;
    dcterms:description "Algren invited Mailer to sit in on a writing class, while Calder brought him to a pioneering writers' conference in Edinburgh. Leone asked him to write a screenplay but concluded he wasn't a cinematic writer. He got Trocchi false papers so he could re-enter Britain. Vidal claimed he hit him with his fist: Mailer said it was a tumbler of ice (they continued to get along, though with bouts of bad blood). He met Moore at a boxing-match, and joined Lowell to march against the Vietnam war. Probably the strongest and fondest of his literary friendships was with Baldwin, written about by Baldwin in a notable essay."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.authorscalendar.info/nmailer.htm>,
        <https://www.theguardian.com/books/2013/dec/02/norman-mailer-double-life-biography-lennon-review> ;
