<https://culturalcartography.net/names/henry-wadsworth-longfellow/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Henry Wadsworth Longfellow" ;
    dcterms:description "He met his lifelong friend Hawthorne as a student; Emerson and Holmes later joined them in a circle of friends in Cambridge (Emerson called him \"a sweet and beautiful soul\"). As a young man he was acquainted with da Ponte. Irving encouraged him; he encouraged Wharton's childhood writing. Whitman knew and liked him, while thinking his poetry innocuous. He wrote a poem in honour of his friend Agassiz's 50th birthday. Dickens was a good friend, Ruskin was very taken by his young daughter, and in old age he visited Tennyson (who took him to be photographed by Julia Margaret Cameron)."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://authorscalendar.info/long.htm>,
        <https://www.poets.org/poet.php/prmPID/143> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q152513 ;
