<https://culturalcartography.net/names/johann-nepomuk-hummel/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Johann Nepomuk Hummel" ;
    dcterms:description "Hummel was a pupil of Haydn, Albrechtsberger, Mozart, Salieri and Clementi. Beethoven, whom he visited regularly, and his former students Czerny and Hiller were among his colleagues; Czerny had been studying with Beethoven but switched to Hummel on hearing him play. Hummel and Hiller were pall-bearers at Beethoven's funeral; he met Schubert at the funeral, who dedicated his last three sonatas to him. He visited Chopin in Poland (both Chopin and Schumann were influenced by him) and Field in Russia."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.allmusic.com/artist/johann-nepomuk-hummel-mn0002137067/biography>,
        <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Johann-Nepomuk-Hummel> ;
