<https://culturalcartography.net/names/raoul-hausmann/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Raoul Hausmann" ;
    dcterms:description "Huelsenbeck helped introduce Hausmann to Dada, but they went on to feud for forty years. Heartfield, Grosz and Baader were fellow-members of the Berlin Dada scene, Richter then arriving from Zürich and Schwitters from Hanover. Schwitters remained a correspondent until his death; Moholy-Nagy and Richter were also lifelong friends to Hausmann. Höch was his lover. He had what Richter described as \"a remarkable, cold-blooded relationship\" with Jung. As a latter-day recluse in France, among his correspondents from a younger generation of artists were Maciunas, Chopin, Spoerri, Johns, Houédard and Themerson."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://monoskop.org/Raoul_Hausmann>,
        <https://www.britannica.com/biography/Raoul-Hausmann> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q84503 ;
