<https://culturalcartography.net/names/morton-feldman/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Morton Feldman" ;
    dcterms:description "Cage and Feldman, who met at a Webern concert, had a close and mutually-significant friendship. Cage introduced him to his painter friends (for five years, the two spent from 6pm to 3am daily talking in the Cedar Bar). He learned a vital lesson walking with Varèse, and studied argumentatively with Wolpe. Guston was his closest friend for two decades, Rauschenberg sold him a painting for $16, and Beckett saw in him the right composer to add music to his texts. As Wolpe advised him of the man in the street's importance, Feldman happened to look down; crossing the road was Pollock."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.biographybase.com/biography/Feldman_Morton.html>,
        <https://www.theguardian.com/music/tomserviceblog/2012/nov/12/morton-feldman-contemporary-music-guide> ;
