<https://culturalcartography.net/names/e-e-cummings/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "E. E. Cummings" ;
    dcterms:description "It may be easy to dismiss Cummings as a precocious modernist who failed to develop much; but he was influential, and Copland (a friend), Cage and Berio all set his words to music. In his childhood, James was a family friend and neighbour, as he himself was later to the young Wolff. Dos Passos was a trusty friend through university and after. Crane, Pound, Stein, MacLeish, Aragon, Thomson and Evans were all met in Paris. Brik tried to indoctrinate him, Tailleferre shared a ride to the south of France and back, Powys was a New York neighbour, and Campos (his translator) was among his many correspondents."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://authorscalendar.info/cummings.htm>,
        <https://www.poets.org/poet.php/prmPID/156> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q298703 ;
