<https://culturalcartography.net/names/mick-jagger/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "Mick Jagger" ;
    dcterms:description "For a good decade, Jagger was a leading counter-cultural icon and thorn in society's side. His fellow-conspirator Richards was first met at primary school — their creative partnership was crucial to the Rolling Stones' success. Waters, Berry and Dixon — strong influences all — came to see them in Chicago; Spector, another significant connection, was also met on their first US trip. Southern and Capote (who wore ear-plugs all the time) both tagged along on tour. Jagger extolled Diddley's generosity of spirit, and was responsible for Wolf's only TV appearance. Godard made a famously incoherent film featuring the Stones."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://www.biography.com/people/mick-jagger-9351966>,
        <https://www.songhall.org/profile/Mick_Jagger> ;
    owl:sameAs wd:Q128121 ;
