<https://culturalcartography.net/names/gyorgy-kepes/#person> a foaf:Person ;
    rdfs:label "György Kepes" ;
    dcterms:description "Kepes did much to found the academic study of visual communication. Both Kassák and Moholy-Nagy were influential mentors — Moholy, initially a correspondent, became a lifelong friend and colleague on both sides of the Atlantic. Kepes' wide circle of intellectually-engaged friends and associates included Albers, Archipenko, Arnheim, Calder, Eames, Fuller, Gabo, Gropius, Mead, Salk, Sert and Wiener. He went for a long walk with Dovzhenko, asked Kodály to write music for a film, had lobster cooked by Hofmann, and a house designed by Breuer (Cage and Cunningham visited). Bass and Tony Smith were among his students."@en ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://act.mit.edu/people/director/gyorgy-kepes/>,
        <https://monoskop.org/György_Kepes> ;
